# tally 2.1.8 R15 (#184), L §5.18: a mean over a known count is its sum scaled by the count, linear in its terms:
# mean(z[k] + x for k in ks) - x is 5 PLN + 0.5 × the hole (a mean of money is a num PLN, as a known mean prints).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [a, b]
input z[k in ks]: money PLN
input x: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  z[a] = 10.00 PLN "s"
  z[b] = ?"z of b" "s"
  x = 4.00 PLN "s"

ask p5: mean(z[k] for k in ks) partial
ask p5b: mean(z[k] + x for k in ks) - x partial
=== expect
p5: 5 PLN + 0.5 × ?"z of b" (z[b])
  cut 2026-06-10
p5b: 5 PLN + 0.5 × ?"z of b" (z[b])
  cut 2026-06-10
